      {
        "content": "Given:\n- The first cooler is 100 liters.\n- The second cooler is 50% bigger than the first.\n- The third cooler is half the size of the second.\n\nLet's calculate the size of each cooler step by step.\n\n1. The first cooler is 100 liters.\n2. The second cooler is 50% bigger than the first:\n   \\[\n   100 \\text{ liters} + 0.5 \\times 100 \\text{ liters} = 100 \\text{ liters} + 50 \\text{ liters} = 150 \\text{ liters}\n   \\]\n3. The third cooler is half the size of the second:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{150 \\text{ liters}}{2} = 75 \\text{ liters}\n   \\]\n\nNow, let's sum the sizes of all three coolers:\n\\[\n100 \\text{ liters} + 150 \\text{ liters} + 75 \\text{ liters} = 325 \\text{ liters}\n\\]\n\nThe total water capacity of the three coolers is 325 liters.\n\nFINAL: 325",
